{
  "info": {
    "name": "Audio Censor API",
    "description": "Requests for the Audio Censor FastAPI app.\n\n**Before running:**\n1. Start the server: `uv run fastapi dev app/main.py` (from the `audio_sensor` folder).\n2. Wait for `Application startup complete`.\n3. If you run on a different port, change the `baseUrl` collection variable.\n\nThe `/censor` requests point at `C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\Downloads\\freesound_community-fuck-36089.mp3`. To use another file, open the request's **Body** tab and pick a file in the `file` row.\n\nFolders run in order: **Auth** signs up a fresh user and logs in (saving `accessToken`); **Censor** and **Audio** send that token, and **Censor** saves the new record's ID as `audioId` for **Audio**. `/censor` and `/audio/*` require login.\n\nUse **Send and Download** (arrow next to Send) to save the censored audio. Each request has checks in its **Tests** tab; results show in the response **Test Results** tab.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "audioId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "signupEmail",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "signupEmailUpper",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "Signup, login and the current user. Run in order: **Sign up** generates a fresh email each run (saved as `signupEmail`), **Log in** saves `accessToken`, and **Get current user** uses it.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sign up",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/signup",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "signup"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{signupEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"correct-horse-42\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Creates an account. Password rules: 8-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, no leading/trailing spaces."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Fresh, mixed-case email per run so this never hits an existing account.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('signupEmail', `Postman.User+${Date.now()}@Example.com`);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Returns id, email, is_active, created_at', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.all.keys('id', 'email', 'is_active', 'created_at');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Email is stored lower-cased', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('signupEmail').toLowerCase());",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Password is never returned', () => pm.expect(pm.response.text().toLowerCase()).to.not.include('password'));",
                  "pm.test('New accounts are active', () => pm.expect(body.is_active).to.be.true);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', body.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
